{"duration_api_ms":4717,"stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"d5a05db6-6fa7-4f09-8896-bdc08c96aca3","total_cost_usd":0.0008189,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1017,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":893,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":556},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1017,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":893,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1017,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1017},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-5-5":{"inputTokens":1560,"outputTokens":919,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":1017,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.0008189,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":128000,"thinkingTokens":556,"cacheCreationEphemeral5mInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationEphemeral1hInputTokens":1017,"canonicalModel":"claude-haiku-5-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"safety_stops":0,"is_error":false,"num_turns":1,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"**No.** An Irish ICAV (Irish Collective Asset-management Vehicle, under the ICAV Act 2015) is a single body corporate with its own legal personality. Its sub-funds are compartments of that entity, not separate legal persons, so they cannot sue, be sued, or contract in their own names. The ICAV acts on their behalf.\n\n**Segregated liability** is statutory rather than inherent. The Act provides that assets attributable to one sub-fund are not available to meet another's liabilities, so creditors generally have recourse only to that sub-fund's assets. Practice is to name the relevant sub-fund in contracts and keep separate books and records.\n\n**The limitation:** segregation depends on the ICAV statutory framework, so its protection is only as strong as a foreign court's willingness to recognise it, which is weaker than true separate personality. Cross-border counterparties and insolvency practitioners in some jurisdictions may test it. Investors and counterparties often mitigate this with contractual provisions and legal opinions.","ttft_ms":3217,"type":"result","duration_ms":4121,"uuid":"6027964e-aa9a-437d-aab5-d3d5498a7b16","ttft_stream_ms":819,"time_to_request_ms":56,"first_content_frame_ms":819,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0,"credential_expires_at":"2026-11-28T06:36:39.484Z"}
